  <section id="your-content">
    <h2>
      Your Content
    </h2>
    <p>
      "Your content" means everything you bring to or make in the app:
      books you import, highlights, notes, thoughts, tags, chats with
      Samwell, goals, daily logs, check-ins, and anything you type.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>You own it.</strong> These terms do
      not give us ownership of your content. It is stored in a local
      database on your device, and we do not keep a copy of it. Because
      of that, we cannot recover it if you lose your device or delete the
      app. Back up what matters to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Permission to process it.</strong>
      When you use Samwell Cloud or another cloud feature, you ask us to
      send the relevant part of your content through our server to the AI
      and other providers that do the work, as described in the <a
        href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a
      >. You give us the limited permission needed to do exactly that, to
      return the result to you, and to keep the usage records the
      Privacy Policy describes. We do not use your content for anything
      else.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your responsibility.</strong> You
      promise that you have the right to use every book, article, audio
      file, and other material you add to the app, and to have it read,
      summarised, quoted, or spoken by the features you use. Open Citadel
      does not check this and does not sell books. Do not add material
      you have no right to use.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Highlight cards and sharing.</strong>
      When you export a highlight or a note as an image or share it, you
      are responsible for what you share and for whether you may share
      it. Quotes from a book remain subject to that book's copyright.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts">
    <h2>
      Accounts &amp; Your Device Identity
    </h2>
    <p>
      You do not need an account to read, highlight, or use on-device
      Samwell. You do not need one to buy a plan, either. Samwell Cloud
      works in two ways:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>With an account.</strong> You sign
        in or register through our sign-in provider, and your plan and
        Neurons belong to that account. This is how you use your plan on
        more than one device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Without an account.</strong> If
        you buy a plan without signing in, the app creates a private
        identity for your device and keeps its secret in your device's
        secure storage. Your plan and Neurons belong to that device
        identity. If you later sign in, the app links the two so your
        plan follows your account.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you buy without an account and then lose the device, reinstall
      the app on Android, or switch phones before you have signed in, we
      may not be able to connect your plan to you again. Signing in and
      restoring purchases from inside the app is how you avoid that. We
      cannot restore something we cannot tie to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Keep your access safe.</strong> You
      are responsible for your sign-in, your device, and what happens
      through them. Tell us promptly if you think someone else has
      access. Accounts and device identities are personal. Do not share
      them, sell them, or let others spend your Neurons.
    </p>
    <p>
      Give us accurate information, and keep your email address current
      so that we can reach you about your account. You can delete your
      account at any time from <strong
        >Settings</strong
      >, or by following <a
        href="/delete-account">Delete Your Account</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="samwell">
    <h2>
      Samwell &amp; AI
    </h2>
    <p>
      Samwell is an artificial intelligence companion. He is not a
      person, a therapist, a coach with credentials, or a substitute for
      one. He is built to help you think, remember, plan, and act on what
      you read, and he works from your reading and the goals you set.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>He can be wrong.</strong> AI models
      make things up, misquote books, misremember what you told them, and
      sound sure when they are not. Check anything that matters,
      especially facts, quotations, dates, figures, and anything you will
      act on. You use Samwell's answers at your own risk.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Two kinds of Samwell.</strong>
      On-device Samwell runs an AI model on your phone, and what you say
      to him stays there. Samwell Cloud runs on larger models hosted by
      others and reached through our server. Cloud replies are generated
      by third-party AI providers, and we do not control what those
      providers' models say. Which models are offered, and to which
      plan, can change. See <a
        href="#availability">Updates &amp; Availability</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What Samwell can do in your app.</strong>
      Samwell can look things up in your library, highlights, notes, and
      goals, and can propose or make changes such as tags, collections,
      your reading queue, and goal check-ins. Many changes wait for your
      approval before they happen. When you explicitly ask Samwell to
      delete a highlight or a note, that deletion is permanent. Read what
      you are approving.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Outputs.</strong> Replies are
      generated for you and may be similar to what other people receive.
      We make no promise that any output is unique, accurate, or fit for
      a particular purpose. As between you and us, you may use the
      replies you receive for your own purposes, subject to these terms
      and to any rights third parties hold in material the replies
      quote.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="not-advice">
    <h2>
      Not Professional Advice
    </h2>
    <p>
      Open Citadel is a tool for reading, reflection, and self-directed
      growth. Compass lets you set goals in areas such as health,
      fitness, learning, career, and relationships, and Samwell talks
      about them with you. None of it is medical, psychological, legal,
      financial, tax, religious, or other professional advice, and it
      does not create a professional relationship.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Speak to a qualified professional before making decisions about
        your health, medication, mental health, money, or legal
        position.
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not start, change, or stop a medical, exercise, or dietary
        plan because of something Samwell said without checking with a
        qualified professional first.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open Citadel is not a crisis service. If you are in danger or
        thinking of harming yourself or someone else, contact your local
        emergency number or a crisis line right away. Do not wait for a
        reply from an app.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="plans">
    <h2>
      Samwell Cloud Plans &amp; Neurons
    </h2>
    <p>
      Samwell Cloud is sold as monthly subscription plans. At the time of
      writing the plans are called Maester, Grand Maester, and
      Archmaester Samwell. Each higher plan reaches more models and
      comes with a bigger monthly allowance. The plans on offer, their
      prices, the models each one reaches, and the size of each
      allowance are shown in the app and in the store before you buy,
      and they can change.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What a Neuron is.</strong> A Neuron
      is the unit we use to meter Samwell Cloud. It is a measure of how
      much of the service you have used, not money. Your plan grants a
      number of Neurons on purchase and on each monthly renewal. When you
      use a cloud feature, the cost of that use is worked out from what
      the underlying provider actually charges us for it and is taken
      from your balance in Neurons. A heavy message on an expensive model
      costs more than a light message on a cheap one. Charges are
      rounded up, and every metered request costs at least one Neuron.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The figures in the app.</strong> The
      app shows estimates before you send a message and your balance
      afterwards. Estimates are only estimates. What you are charged is
      settled after the work is done, and it can be higher or lower than
      the estimate. Your balance in the app is the figure that counts.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Rollover.</strong> Some unused
      Neurons carry over to the next month, up to a cap that is a share
      of your plan's monthly allowance and is shown in the app. Anything
      above the cap is lost when your plan renews.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What Neurons are not.</strong>
      Neurons have no cash value. They cannot be exchanged for money,
      transferred to another person, or sold. They are a licence to use
      the service, not property. They are not refundable. You need an
      active plan to spend them, and unused Neurons may be removed after
      your plan lapses or when your account is deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Limits on a single message.</strong>
      To protect you from a runaway request, a single message has a
      ceiling on how many Neurons it may spend and on how many times
      Samwell may look things up while answering. If a message reaches a
      ceiling, it stops and you are told. The Neurons already used are
      charged, because the work was done.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Running out.</strong> If your
      balance is too low for a request, or you have no active plan, the
      request is refused. On-device Samwell and the rest of the app keep
      working.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="payments">
    <h2>
      Billing, Renewal &amp; Refunds
    </h2>
    <p>
      <strong>The store sells it.</strong> Plans
      are bought through Google Play or the App Store. The store
      processes the payment under its own terms, and we never see or
      store your card or payment details. We use RevenueCat to manage
      subscriptions and to tell which plan you are on.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Prices and tax.</strong> The price
      shown in the store at the moment of purchase is the price you
      pay, in your local currency, and it may include taxes that the
      store adds.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Auto-renewal.</strong> A plan is a
      subscription that renews every month until you cancel it. Your
      store account is charged when you buy and again at each renewal,
      usually within 24 hours before the current period ends. Your
      Neurons for the new month are granted when the store confirms the
      renewal.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Cancelling.</strong> You cancel in
      the store, not in the app and not with us: in the Google Play app
      under Subscriptions, or on iPhone under Settings, your name, then
      Subscriptions. Cancel at least a day before the renewal date to
      avoid the next charge. When you cancel, you keep your plan until
      the end of the period you have already paid for.
      <strong
        >Deleting your account or uninstalling the app does not cancel a
        subscription.</strong
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Changing plans.</strong> You can
      move between plans in the store. How the change is charged and when
      it takes effect is decided by the store, and the app shows what
      you are getting before you confirm.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Price changes.</strong> We may
      change the price of a plan. A price change applies at your next
      renewal, and the store will notify you and may ask for your
      consent. If you do not accept it, cancel before the renewal.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Refunds.</strong> We do not take
      payment ourselves, so we cannot issue refunds ourselves. Google
      Play and the App Store handle refund requests under their own
      policies, and the decision is theirs. Request a refund from the
      store you bought from. Where the law gives you a right to a refund
      or a cooling-off period, that right is not affected by this
      section. Spent Neurons cannot be returned, because the work they
      paid for has already been done.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="insider-codes">
    <h2>
      Insider Codes
    </h2>
    <p>
      From time to time we may give people an insider code. A code
      grants a plan for a set time, such as a day, a week, a month, or a
      year, and your Neurons for that plan are granted monthly until the
      time is up. You redeem a code in Settings.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A code can be used once. Do not share it, post it, or sell it.
      </li>
      <li>
        It has no cash value, cannot be exchanged for money, and does
        not renew. When the time ends, the plan ends.
      </li>
      <li>
        A code is a gift, not a purchase. We may withdraw one, and end
        the access it gave, if it was obtained or used in breach of these
        terms.
      </li>
      <li>
        All the other terms on this page apply to access gained through a
        code.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="cloud-features">
    <h2>
      Voices, Transcripts &amp; Web Search
    </h2>
    <p>
      Besides chat, some cloud features use your plan and spend Neurons.
      They are provided by third-party AI providers through our server
      and are described in the <a
        href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a
      >.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloud reading voices.</strong>
        Natural voices that read a book or article aloud. What you spend
        depends on how much text is read and on the voice you choose.
        Voices available to you depend on your plan, and a voice can be
        added, changed, or removed. You use the phone's built-in voice
        for free.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Podcast transcripts.</strong>
        Turning an episode into text. The cost depends on the length of
        the episode. Very long episodes may be refused. Transcripts are
        machine made and can contain errors, including wrong words and
        wrong speaker names.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Web search.</strong> Samwell Cloud
        can search the web to answer you. Results come from other
        people's websites. We do not check or endorse them, and the
        search itself costs Neurons.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To keep the service fast and fair for everyone, some features have
      fair use limits, such as limits on how many requests can run at
      once, how much can be requested in a day, or how long a piece can
      be. We may apply and change these limits, and a request over a
      limit may be refused.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-party-content">
    <h2>
      Free Books, Podcasts &amp; Blogs
    </h2>
    <p>
      Open Citadel is a reader and a companion. It is not a publisher or
      a bookshop. It gives you ways to read what you bring or choose, and
      it does not own, review, or take responsibility for that material.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Free books.</strong> The app can
        find and download free books from Project Gutenberg. A book that
        is free to read in one country is not always free everywhere.
        You are responsible for making sure that downloading and using a
        book is lawful where you are.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Podcasts and blogs.</strong> You
        add feeds, shows, and articles yourself. Their content belongs to
        the people who made it and is under their terms. We do not host,
        copy, or edit it for you beyond what is needed to show it in the
        app, and we are not responsible for what it says.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your own files.</strong> Use books
        and audio that you own or have the right to use. Do not use the
        app to copy or share material in a way the owner has not allowed.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Summaries, transcripts, and audio that you create from someone
      else's material are for your own private use. They do not give you
      any right to publish or share that material.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="on-device-models">
    <h2>
      On-Device Models
    </h2>
    <p>
      On-device Samwell runs an AI model stored on your phone. You choose
      which model to download inside the app. Models are made by other
      people, and each is offered under its maker's own licence and terms,
      which apply to you when you download and use it. We do not control
      those licences or the models.
    </p>
    <p>
      Models are large. Downloading one uses your data and storage, and
      running one uses battery and may make your phone warm or slow.
      Whether a model runs well depends on your device. On-device
      models are smaller than cloud models and are more likely to give
      weaker or wrong answers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use">
    <h2>
      Acceptable Use
    </h2>
    <p>
      Use the app and the service fairly and lawfully. You agree not to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>break any law, or the rights of anyone else, using the app;</li>
      <li>
        use Samwell Cloud to make content that is illegal, that exploits
        or sexualises children, that promotes violence or hatred, or that
        is meant to harass, defraud, or deceive;
      </li>
      <li>
        try to get around Neuron metering, plan limits, per-message
        ceilings, or fair use limits, or use the service without paying
        for what it costs;
      </li>
      <li>
        share, sell, or pool an account, a device identity, or an insider
        code, or let someone else spend your Neurons;
      </li>
      <li>
        send automated, bulk, or scripted requests to the service, or use
        it as a free way into AI providers, unless we have agreed to it
        in writing;
      </li>
      <li>
        use the service or its replies to build or train a competing
        product or a machine learning model;
      </li>
      <li>
        attack, overload, probe for weaknesses in, or break into the
        service, other users' accounts, or our providers' systems;
      </li>
      <li>
        try to pull out the hidden instructions, keys, or private
        workings of the service, or to make Samwell act against its
        purpose; or
      </li>
      <li>
        encourage or help anyone else to do any of the above.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you break these rules, we may refuse requests, limit your
      access, or suspend or end your account, as described in <a
        href="#termination">Ending Your Use</a
      >. Our AI providers also have usage policies, and they may refuse
      a request or report abuse without us being able to prevent it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="open-source">
    <h2>
      Open Source &amp; Our Rights
    </h2>
    <p>
      The source code of Open Citadel is published under the GNU Affero
      General Public License, version 3 or later, at <a
        href={GITHUB_URL}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">our GitHub repository</a
      >. That licence, and not these terms, decides what you may do with
      the source code. Nothing here restricts a right the AGPL gives you.
    </p>
    <p>What the AGPL does not give you:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The service.</strong> Our hosted
        server, accounts, plans, Neurons, and the agreements we have with
        AI and other providers are not part of the code. You cannot use
        our service, or our keys and accounts with other providers,
        except through these terms.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our names and marks.</strong>
        "Open Citadel", "Samwell", the app's icon, and its branding are
